  tool='write' path='/02_distill/cards/agentic-surfaces-conversion-gap.md' content="# Agentic surfaces lose on conversion vs. owned environments\n\n**Source:** [/01_capture/influential/2026-03-23__hn-walmart-chatgpt-checkout.md](/01_capture/influential/2026-03-23__hn-walmart-chatgpt-checkout.md)\n\n## Key insight\n\nWalmart's test of ChatGPT Instant Checkout (200k items) showed **1/3 conversion rate** vs. website checkout. The in-chat experience felt unsatisfying despite technical viability.\n\n## The gap\n\nTechnical implementation ≠ conversion success. Third-party chat surfaces lose when:\n- Trust is weaker (not your own domain)\n- Product context is thin (chat isn't built for browsing)\n- Purchase flow fragmentation (user leaves the surface to complete checkout)\n\n## Strategic implication\n\nMerchants stay in control of identity, cart sync, and checkout. The assistant becomes a *helper within the owned environment*, not a replacement surface.\n\n**Related:** Agent tooling, merchant trust, agentic UX design\n" start_line=0 end_line=0
