  tool='write' path='/02_distill/cards/agent-kernel-markdown-git-memory.md' content="# Agent Kernel: Markdown + Git as Memory System\n\n- **Source:** [/01_capture/influential/2026-03-23__hn-agent-kernel.md](/01_capture/influential/2026-03-23__hn-agent-kernel.md)\n- **Date:** 2026-03-23\n- **People:** Oguz Bilgic\n- **Topics:** agent memory, stateful agents, minimal architecture, git-based versioning, markdown, AGENTS.md pattern\n\n## Key Points\n- Agent Kernel uses three markdown files (AGENTS.md, IDENTITY.md, KNOWLEDGE.md) plus git as the entire memory system—zero framework, zero database\n- Memory split across kernel (rules), identity (who), knowledge index, state folder (current), and append-only session logs\n- Git provides versioning, durability, and history without external infrastructure\n- HN feedback highlights simplicity as strength but append-only logs risk polluting future context\n- Architectural criticism: instruction files weaker than enforced hooks for behavior that must be guaranteed\n\n## Why this matters for current work\n- This repo uses AGENTS.md-based approach; Agent Kernel validates the pattern but highlights scaling concerns\n- Append-only session logs are a real pollution risk as agent runs accumulate\n- The tension between instruction-as-guidance vs. enforced hooks is relevant to any AGENTS.md system\n- Validates recoverability-first approach (git + text) over perfect access\n\n<!-- AGENT_EDITABLE_START:reflection -->\n- AGENTS.md as kernel mirrors this pattern; strength is simplicity and recoverability, weakness is reliance on agent compliance rather than enforced constraints\n- Append-only notes problem suggests need for active cleanup mechanisms, not just passive instruction\n- Zero-database approach aligns with this repo's philosophy but requires discipline on log management\n<!-- AGENT_EDITABLE_END:reflection -->\n" start_line=0 end_line=0
